<LegalLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How Drivebase handles your data across the open-source self-hosted app and the managed cloud service."
	updated="June 2, 2026"
>
	<p>
		Drivebase is an open-source, self-hostable platform that connects your cloud
		storage providers under one interface. This policy explains what data we
		handle and how — and it draws a clear line between the <strong>self-hosted</strong>
		software and the <strong>managed cloud service</strong> at
		<a href="https://cloud.drivebase.io">cloud.drivebase.io</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Self-hosted Drivebase</h2>
	<p>
		When you run Drivebase on your own infrastructure, your data never reaches
		us. Everything — provider credentials, file metadata, and operation history —
		lives in the database you control. We do not receive telemetry, file contents,
		or account information from self-hosted instances.
	</p>

	<h2>Managed cloud service</h2>
	<p>
		If you use the hosted service at cloud.drivebase.io, we process a limited
		amount of data to provision and run your instance:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Account data</strong> — your email address and authentication details, used to sign you in and contact you about your account.</li>
		<li><strong>Billing data</strong> — subscription and payment information is processed by our payment provider, <a href="https://polar.sh">Polar</a>. We do not store full card details on our servers.</li>
		<li><strong>Instance metadata</strong> — the plan you are on and the resources allocated to your instance, used for provisioning, support, and billing.</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Storage provider credentials</h3>
	<p>
		Credentials you connect (Google Drive, Amazon S3, Dropbox, and others) are
		stored within your own Drivebase instance so it can talk to those providers
		on your behalf. We do not browse, copy, or sell the contents of your files.
	</p>

	<h2>Analytics</h2>
	<p>
		On this website we use privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics to understand
		aggregate traffic (such as page views and referrers). It does not track you
		across sites or build an advertising profile.
	</p>

	<h2>Data sharing</h2>
	<p>
		We do not sell your personal data. We share information only with the service
		providers needed to run the cloud offering — for example, our payment
		processor and hosting infrastructure — and only to the extent required to
		deliver the service.
	</p>

	<h2>Your choices</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>You can delete your cloud account and instance at any time, which removes the associated account and instance data.</li>
		<li>You can disconnect any storage provider from within Drivebase.</li>
		<li>Self-hosting gives you full control: export, migrate, or delete your data directly.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Changes</h2>
	<p>
		We may update this policy as the product evolves. Material changes will be
		reflected by the "last updated" date above.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about privacy? Reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@drivebase.io">hello@drivebase.io</a>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
